module lib/hf/tests/md_onebody
  The checks of lib/hf/md_onebody against reference data, and their helpers.

md1_prims_case  @96e1e64a
  PS      the shell rows of lib/hfref/prims: angular momentum, exponent and center
  CH      the position of the point charge of each case
  c       the case
  atoms   the atoms pack being filled: two uncharged centers and the charge
  shells  the shell pack being filled: one single-primitive shell per center
  pr      the primitive pack returned
  off     the index the next shell's first basis function gets
  k       which of the two shells is being written
  row     its row of `PS`
  l       its angular momentum

md1_prims_fix  @9132f81e
  why   A test against a reference is only as good as the reference; where
        PySCF's own value is the less accurate one, the test compares with
        the high-precision value instead.

md1_prims_ref  @31d87df1
  FX    the replacement table from md1_prims_fix, flat
  c     the case
  k     the pick
  kind  `0` for S, `1` for T, `2` for V
  ref   PySCF's value
  r     the replacement row being compared

md1_prims_worst  @f5b311c4
  why   One-shell-pair cases up to f functions reach every branch of
        md1_pair (every power shift of the kinetic energy, every Hermite
        order of V) with no other shell pair in the sum, so a wrong term shows up
        in the case that exercises it.
  PS    the shell rows of the cases
  CH    the point charge of each case
  PK    the component pair each pick reads
  RS    PySCF's overlap values
  RT    PySCF's kinetic energy values
  RV    PySCF's nuclear attraction values
  FX    the replacement references
  ws    the worst relative gap of S so far
  wt    the same for T
  wv    the same for V
  nrep  how many replacement references were used
  ntest how many values were tested
  c     the case
  atoms the case's atoms pack
  shells the case's shell pack
  pr    the case's primitive pack
  cn    its normalized contraction coefficients
  G     its Boys grid
  B     the pair block md1_pair computes for the case
  nb    the second shell's number of components
  k     the pick
  r     the pick's row in the reference tables
  col   the column of the block the pick reads
  rs    the overlap reference
  rt    the kinetic energy reference
  rv    the nuclear attraction reference
  hs    `1` when the overlap reference was replaced
  ht    the same for the kinetic energy
  hv    the same for the nuclear attraction

  = md1_prims_case()  the case's two shells and the point charge
  = md1_pair()  S, T and V for the case, as one block
  = md1_prims_ref()  the reference for each value: PySCF's, or the high-precision one where PySCF is off
